<h3 id=3D"7-gateway-webhook-internal" data-toc=3D"7. Gateway Webhook (inter=
nal)">7. Gateway Webhook (internal)</h3>
<div class=3D"endpoint"><span class=3D"m m-post">POST</span><code>/internal=
/gateway/webhooks</code></div>
<p>The payment gateway calls this when a top-up payment succeeds or fails. =
We verify the HMAC signature, then <strong>re-fetch the payment status from=
 the gateway's API</strong> before crediting anything. The same event can a=
rrive several times.</p>
<div class=3D"callout tip"><div class=3D"ct">Why amounts in paise, and why =
an Idempotency-Key on every POST?</div><p>Integers make every sum exact, an=
d the key lets the server recognise a retry of the same user action and ret=
urn the first result instead of moving money again (Deep Dive 5).</p></div>
</section>

<section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"data-model" data-toc=3D"5. Database Schema=
"><span class=3D"sec-n">5.</span> Data Model</h2>
<p class=3D"lead">MySQL 8 (InnoDB), sharded by <code>wallet_id</code>. Ever=
ything about one wallet (its balance, its ledger entries, its idempotency k=
eys) lives on the <strong>same shard</strong>, so a single-wallet operation=
 is one local ACID transaction.</p>
<h3 id=3D"1-why-a-ledger-and-not-just-a-balance-column" data-toc=3D"1. Why =
a Ledger and not just a Balance Column?">1. Why a Ledger and not just a Bal=
ance Column?</h3>
<p>A <strong>double-entry ledger</strong> records every movement as at leas=
t two entries: a <strong>debit</strong> from one account and a <strong>cred=
it</strong> to another, of equal amounts. Money is never created or destroy=
ed, only moved. The wallet's <code>balance</code> column is a cached sum of=
 its entries, updated in the same transaction.</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table><thead><tr><th>Transaction</th><th>Account</th><t=
h>Debit</th><th>Credit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Asha adds =E2=82=B91=
,000 by UPI</td><td>gateway_clearing (system)</td><td>=E2=82=B91,000</td><t=
d></td></tr><tr><td></td><td>wallet: Asha</td><td></td><td>=E2=82=B91,000</=
td></tr><tr class=3D"hl"><td>Asha sends Ravi =E2=82=B9500</td><td>wallet: A=
sha</td><td>=E2=82=B9500</td><td></td></tr><tr class=3D"hl"><td></td><td>wa=
llet: Ravi</td><td></td><td>=E2=82=B9500</td></tr><tr><td>Ravi withdraws =
=E2=82=B9300</td><td>wallet: Ravi</td><td>=E2=82=B9300</td><td></td></tr><t=
r><td></td><td>payout_clearing (system)</td><td></td><td>=E2=82=B9300</td><=
/tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Every row pair sums to zero. Summing all entries for Asha gives her bala=
nce (=E2=82=B91,000 =E2=88=92 =E2=82=B9500 =3D =E2=82=B9500); summing every=
 account in the system always gives zero. That makes errors <strong>detecta=
ble</strong> (Deep Dive 12), which a single mutable balance column never is=
.</p>
