<div class=3D"callout tip"><div class=3D"ct">System accounts live on every =
shard</div><p>Each shard has its own <code>gateway_clearing</code>, <code>p=
ayout_clearing</code> and <code>transfer_clearing</code> rows. A top-up for=
 a wallet on shard 7 debits shard 7's <code>gateway_clearing</code>, so it =
stays a local transaction, and no single system row becomes a global hotspo=
t.</p></div>
<h3 id=3D"3-which-database-and-why" data-toc=3D"3. Which database, and why?=
">3. Which database, and why?</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table><thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Store</th><th>Why</th=
></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Wallets, ledger, transactions, idempotency, ou=
tbox</td><td>MySQL 8 InnoDB, 16 shards; each a primary + semi-sync replica<=
/td><td>ACID, row locks, CHECK constraints, mature tooling; money needs mul=
ti-row transactions</td></tr><tr><td>Balance cache, rate limits</td><td>Red=
is</td><td>display-only balance, per-user request limits</td></tr><tr><td>W=
allet events</td><td>Kafka (partitioned by wallet id)</td><td>fan-out to no=
tifications, history, risk, analytics</td></tr><tr><td>History read model</=
td><td>MySQL read replicas, or Cassandra at larger scale</td><td>keeps heav=
y history queries off the primaries</td></tr><tr><td>Archive (&gt; 13 month=
s)</td><td>Object storage (Parquet) + warehouse</td><td>cheap 10-year reten=
tion for audit</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</section>

