<h3 id=3D"1-api-gateway" data-toc=3D"1. API Gateway">1. API Gateway</h3>
<p>Terminates TLS, authenticates the user and device, applies per-user and =
per-merchant rate limits, and rejects any money-moving <code>POST</code> wi=
thout an <code>Idempotency-Key</code>. Routes to the services. Stateless; s=
cales horizontally.</p>
<h3 id=3D"2-wallet-service" data-toc=3D"2. Wallet Service">2. Wallet Servic=
e</h3>
<p>Owns wallets: creation, KYC level, freeze / unfreeze, limits and balance=
 reads. Knows the <strong>shard map</strong> (<code>wallet_id =E2=86=92 sha=
rd</code>) and is the only code allowed to write <code>wallets</code> and <=
code>ledger_entries</code>. Other services call its internal "post entries"=
 operation, which runs one local transaction on one shard.</p>
<h3 id=3D"3-transfer-service" data-toc=3D"3. Transfer Service">3. Transfer =
Service</h3>
<p>Handles pay and send. If both wallets are on the same shard it runs one =
local ACID transaction (Flow 1). If not, it coordinates a cross-shard trans=
fer as a <strong>saga</strong> with a durable state machine (Flow 2, Deep D=
ive 4). Also handles refunds.</p>
<h3 id=3D"4-top-up-service" data-toc=3D"4. Top-up Service">4. Top-up Servic=
e</h3>
<p>Creates gateway orders, receives signed webhooks, verifies the payment s=
tatus with the gateway, and credits the wallet exactly once. Polls the gate=
way for payments whose webhook never arrived.</p>
<h3 id=3D"5-payout-service" data-toc=3D"5. Payout Service">5. Payout Servic=
e</h3>
<p>Reserves the money, calls the bank payout API with our withdrawal id as =
the reference, and settles or reverses based on the bank's final answer. Ne=
ver treats a timeout as a failure.</p>
<h3 id=3D"6-statement-service" data-toc=3D"6. Statement Service">6. Stateme=
nt Service</h3>
<p>Serves history and monthly statements from the History Store, a read mod=
el built from Kafka events. Keeps heavy, paginated queries off the shard pr=
imaries.</p>
<h3 id=3D"7-wallet-db-mysql-shards" data-toc=3D"7. Wallet DB (MySQL shards)=
">7. Wallet DB (MySQL shards)</h3>
<p>16 shards by <code>wallet_id</code>. Each shard is a primary with a <str=
ong>semi-synchronous</strong> replica (a commit returns only after the repl=
ica has the binlog), plus <code>innodb_flush_log_at_trx_commit=3D1</code> a=
nd <code>sync_binlog=3D1</code>, so a committed payment survives losing the=
 primary.</p>
<h3 id=3D"8-kafka-notification-risk-reconciliation" data-toc=3D"8. Kafka, N=
otification, Risk, Reconciliation">8. Kafka, Notification, Risk, Reconcilia=
tion</h3>
<p>An outbox relay (CDC on the binlog, e.g. Debezium) publishes every commi=
tted movement to Kafka, keyed by wallet id. Consumers send notifications, u=
pdate the history store, score fraud, and feed analytics. Reconciliation ru=
ns daily against gateway and bank settlement files.</p>
</section>

<section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"detailed-design" data-toc=3D"7. Detailed D=
esign (Flows)"><span class=3D"sec-n">7.</span> Detailed Design</h2>
