<p>Asha is on shard 3 and Ravi on shard 9. No single database transaction c=
an cover both rows. The Transfer Service runs a <strong>saga</strong>:</p>
<ol class=3D"nl"><li><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><stro=
ng>T1 on shard 3:</strong> debit Asha and credit shard 3's <code>transfer_c=
learing</code> account (the books still balance on shard 3), insert the <co=
de>transfers</code> row with state <code>DEBITED</code>. One local transact=
ion; the idempotency key lives here.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">2<=
/span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>T2 on shard 9:</strong> insert <code>a=
pplied_transfers(txn_id)</code> (primary key =E2=86=92 applying twice is im=
possible), debit shard 9's <code>transfer_clearing</code>, credit Ravi.</p>=
</div></li><li><span class=3D"n">3</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>T3 =
on shard 3:</strong> mark the transfer <code>COMPLETED</code>. Return 201.<=
/p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">4</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>=
Crash anywhere?</strong> A recovery worker scans <code>transfers</code> row=
s stuck in <code>DEBITED</code> and simply retries T2 (safe because it's id=
empotent), then T3.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">5</span><div class=
=3D"li-b"><p><strong>T2 fails permanently</strong> (Ravi's wallet frozen, o=
r this credit would break his cap): compensate on shard 3: credit Asha back=
 from <code>transfer_clearing</code>, state <code>REVERSED</code>.</p></div=
></li></ol>
<p>Why a saga and not two-phase commit, and what 2PC would look like, is <s=
trong>Deep Dive 4</strong>.</p>
