<h3 id=3D"flow-5-refund-a-payment" data-toc=3D"Flow 5: Refund">Flow 5: Refu=
nd a Payment</h3>
<p>A refund is a <strong>new transaction</strong> in the opposite direction=
 (merchant =E2=86=92 user) that references the original payment. The origin=
al is never edited.</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- on the merchant&#x27;s shard: cap tot=
al refunds at the paid amount, atomically</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> transactions <span class=3D"hljs=
-keyword">SET</span> refunded_minor <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span=
> refunded_minor <span class=3D"hljs-operator">+</span> :amt
 <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> txn_id <span class=3D"hljs-opera=
tor">=3D</span> :orig <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">AND</span> type <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;TRANSFER=
&#x27;</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">AND</span> status <span class=3D=
"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;COMPLETED&#x27=
;</span>
   <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">AND</span> refunded_minor <span class=3D"hl=
js-operator">+</span> :amt <span class=3D"hljs-operator">&lt;=3D</span> amo=
unt_minor;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- 0 rows =E2=86=92 REFUND_EXCEEDS_PAYMENT. 1 =
row =E2=86=92 debit merchant, credit user</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- (same shard: same transaction; different sh=
ards: the same saga as Flow 2)</span></code></pre></div>
<ul class=3D"bl"><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p>Two concurrent partial refunds =
can't over-refund: the conditional <code>UPDATE</code> serializes them on t=
he original row.</p></div></li><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p>If the merchant's=
 balance is too low (already settled to their bank), the refund fails with =
<code>INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS</code> and the merchant tops up; a platform-funded=
 refund would debit a system account instead.</p></div></li></ul>
<h3 id=3D"flow-6-balance-history-reads" data-toc=3D"Flow 6: Balance &amp; h=
istory">Flow 6: Balance & History Reads</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table><thead><tr><th>Read</th><th>Served from</th><th>F=
reshness</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Balance used to approve a debit</t=
d><td>shard primary, inside the debit transaction</td><td>exact</td></tr><t=
r><td>Balance on the home screen</td><td>Redis (key =3D wallet id, value =
=3D balance + version), refreshed from Kafka; miss =E2=86=92 primary</td><t=
d>=E2=89=A4 ~1 s</td></tr><tr><td>Transaction history</td><td>History Store=
, keyset pagination on <code>(wallet_id, entry_id)</code></td><td>=E2=89=A4=
 ~1=E2=80=932 s</td></tr><tr><td>Right after the user's own payment</td><td=
>the API response already carries <code>balanceAfterMinor</code>; the app s=
hows that</td><td>read-your-writes</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class=3D"callout interview"><div class=3D"ct">=F0=9F=92=AC Interview l=
ine</div><p>"Only the debit path needs the exact balance, and it gets it fo=
r free because the check is inside the debit's UPDATE. Everything users mer=
ely look at comes from a cache or a read model that lags by about a second.=
"</p></div>
</section>

<section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"deep-dives" data-toc=3D"8. Deep Dives"><sp=
an class=3D"sec-n">8.</span> Deep Dives</h2>
<p class=3D"lead">The follow-ups an interviewer will push on: locking, dead=
locks, cross-shard atomicity, exactly-once, and the external systems that c=
an fail in strange ways.</p>

<h3 id=3D"deep-dive-1-why-a-double-entry-ledger-isnt-a-balance-column-enoug=
h" class=3D"dd" data-toc=3D"Deep Dive 1: Why a double-entry ledger?"><span =
class=3D"dd-n">Deep Dive 1</span><span class=3D"dd-q">Why a double-entry le=
dger? Isn't a balance column enough?</span></h3>
<p>Three ways to store "how much money does Asha have":</p>
<h4 class=3D"approach"><span class=3D"ap-tag">Approach 1</span>Only a mutab=
le <code>balance</code> column</h4>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> wallets <span class=3D"hlj=
s-keyword">SET</span> balance_minor <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span=
> balance_minor <span class=3D"hljs-operator">-</span> <span class=3D"hljs-=
number">50000</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> wallet_id <s=
pan class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> :asha;</code></pre></div>
<ol class=3D"nl"><li class=3D"pro"><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"=
li-b"><p><strong>Pros:</strong> simplest; balance read is one primary-key l=
ookup.</p></div></li><li class=3D"con"><span class=3D"n">2</span><div class=
=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Cons:</strong> no history of <em>why</em> the balance =
is what it is. A bug that subtracts twice is invisible and unrecoverable. A=
uditors and regulators will not accept it.</p></div></li></ol>
<h4 class=3D"approach"><span class=3D"ap-tag">Approach 2</span>Only a ledge=
r; balance =3D <code>SUM(entries)</code> on every read</h4>
<ol class=3D"nl"><li class=3D"pro"><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"=
li-b"><p><strong>Pros:</strong> the ledger is the single source of truth; n=
othing to drift.</p></div></li><li class=3D"con"><span class=3D"n">2</span>=
<div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Cons:</strong> summing a wallet with 50,000 =
entries on every debit is slow, and the "check then insert" still needs a l=
ock to prevent double spend.</p></div></li></ol>
<h4 class=3D"approach"><span class=3D"ap-tag">Approach 3</span>Ledger + cac=
hed balance, updated in the same transaction</h4>
<ol class=3D"nl"><li class=3D"pro"><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"=
li-b"><p><strong>Pros:</strong> fast exact reads (one row), full history, a=
nd drift is detectable: <code>balance_minor</code> must equal the sum of en=
tries, and each entry carries <code>balance_after_minor</code>, so an audit=
 can walk the chain.</p></div></li><li class=3D"con"><span class=3D"n">2</s=
pan><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Cons:</strong> two writes per account pe=
r movement; the code must always write both (enforce by only allowing write=
s through one "post entries" function).</p></div></li></ol>
<div class=3D"callout "><div class=3D"ct">=E2=9C=85 Our choice</div><p>Appr=
oach 3. The ledger is append-only (no <code>UPDATE</code> / <code>DELETE</c=
ode> privileges on <code>ledger_entries</code> for the app user). Mistakes =
are fixed with a new <strong>reversing transaction</strong>, so history alw=
ays shows what happened and when.</p></div>
<ul class=3D"bl"><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Every transaction balan=
ces:</strong> sum of debits =3D sum of credits, checked in code before comm=
it and again by reconciliation.</p></div></li><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p><s=
trong>System accounts</strong> (<code>gateway_clearing</code>, <code>payout=
_clearing</code>, <code>transfer_clearing</code>, <code>fees_revenue</code>=
) represent money owed to / by the outside world, so even top-ups and withd=
rawals are balanced pairs.</p></div></li><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong=
>Available vs ledger balance:</strong> <code>available =3D balance_minor =
=E2=88=92 held_minor</code>. Holds reserve money without moving it.</p></di=
v></li></ul>
<div class=3D"callout interview"><div class=3D"ct">=F0=9F=92=AC Interview l=
ine</div><p>"I store money as a double-entry ledger: every movement is a de=
bit and an equal credit, entries are append-only, and the wallet balance is=
 a cached sum updated in the same transaction, so it's fast to read and pro=
vably consistent with the history."</p></div>
