<p>The bug is the gap between <strong>reading</strong> the balance and <str=
ong>writing</strong> it. Any fix has to make "check and debit" one indivisi=
ble step for that wallet.</p>
<h4 class=3D"approach"><span class=3D"ap-tag">Approach 1</span>Pessimistic =
lock: <code>SELECT =E2=80=A6 FOR UPDATE</code></h4>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">START</span> TRANSACTION;
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> balance_minor, held_minor <span =
class=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</span> wallets <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHE=
RE</span> wallet_id <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> :asha <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-keyword">FOR</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span>;=
  <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- request 2 waits here</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- app checks balance - held &gt;=3D 40000, th=
en:</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> wallets <span class=3D"hljs-keyw=
ord">SET</span> balance_minor <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> bala=
nce_minor <span class=3D"hljs-operator">-</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number=
">40000</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> wallet_id <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> :asha;
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INT=
O</span> ledger_entries =E2=80=A6;
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">COMMIT</span>;                                =
                                              <span class=3D"hljs-comment">=
-- request 2 now reads 10000 =E2=86=92 rejected</span></code></pre></div>
<ol class=3D"nl"><li class=3D"pro"><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"=
li-b"><p><strong>Pros:</strong> obviously correct; the second request waits=
 and then sees =E2=82=B9100.</p></div></li><li class=3D"con"><span class=3D=
"n">2</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Cons:</strong> lock held across =
an extra round trip between app and DB; if the app pauses (GC, slow network=
) everyone else waits for that wallet.</p></div></li></ol>
<h4 class=3D"approach"><span class=3D"ap-tag">Approach 2</span>Atomic condi=
tional UPDATE (check inside the write)</h4>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> wallets
   <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SET</span> balance_minor <span class=3D"hlj=
s-operator">=3D</span> balance_minor <span class=3D"hljs-operator">-</span>=
 <span class=3D"hljs-number">40000</span>, version <span class=3D"hljs-oper=
ator">=3D</span> version <span class=3D"hljs-operator">+</span> <span class=
=3D"hljs-number">1</span>
 <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> wallet_id <span class=3D"hljs-op=
erator">=3D</span> :asha <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">AND</span> status <sp=
an class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;ACT=
IVE&#x27;</span>
   <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">AND</span> balance_minor <span class=3D"hlj=
s-operator">-</span> held_minor <span class=3D"hljs-operator">&gt;=3D</span=
> <span class=3D"hljs-number">40000</span>;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- rows affected =3D 1 =E2=86=92 debited.  0 =
=E2=86=92 insufficient funds (or frozen)</span></code></pre></div>
<ol class=3D"nl"><li class=3D"pro"><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"=
li-b"><p><strong>Pros:</strong> one statement, one round trip. InnoDB's <co=
de>UPDATE</code> is a <em>locking read</em>: it takes an exclusive lock on =
the row and evaluates the <code>WHERE</code> against the <strong>latest com=
mitted</strong> version (not the transaction's snapshot), so the second req=
uest waits, re-evaluates against =E2=82=B9100, and matches 0 rows.</p></div=
></li><li class=3D"con"><span class=3D"n">2</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><s=
trong>Cons:</strong> you learn only "0 rows", so read the row afterwards if=
 you need the reason (frozen vs insufficient).</p></div></li></ol>
<h4 class=3D"approach"><span class=3D"ap-tag">Approach 3</span>Optimistic l=
ocking with a version column</h4>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> balance_minor, held_minor,=
 version <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</span> wallets <span class=3D"hl=
js-keyword">WHERE</span> wallet_id <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span>=
 :asha;   <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- version =3D 41</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> wallets <span class=3D"hljs-keyw=
ord">SET</span> balance_minor <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> :new=
_balance, version <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"h=
ljs-number">42</span>
 <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> wallet_id <span class=3D"hljs-op=
erator">=3D</span> :asha <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">AND</span> version <s=
pan class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">41</span=
>;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- 0 rows =E2=86=92 someone else changed the w=
allet; re-read and retry (max 3 times)</span></code></pre></div>
<ol class=3D"nl"><li class=3D"pro"><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"=
li-b"><p><strong>Pros:</strong> no lock held while the app thinks; good whe=
n conflicts are rare.</p></div></li><li class=3D"con"><span class=3D"n">2</=
span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Cons:</strong> under contention (a busy=
 merchant, a sale) most attempts fail and retry, so throughput collapses ex=
actly when you need it.</p></div></li></ol>
<h4 class=3D"approach"><span class=3D"ap-tag">Approach 4</span>Distributed =
lock in Redis around the wallet</h4>
<ol class=3D"nl"><li class=3D"pro"><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"=
li-b"><p><strong>Pros:</strong> can serialize work that spans several syste=
ms.</p></div></li><li class=3D"con"><span class=3D"n">2</span><div class=3D=
"li-b"><p><strong>Cons:</strong> Redis locks have expiry: if the holder pau=
ses longer than the TTL, two holders can run at once, unless every write ch=
ecks a fencing token. The database must still enforce the rule, so the Redi=
s lock adds a dependency without removing the DB check.</p></div></li></ol>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Read-check-write</th><th>=
FOR UPDATE</th><th>Conditional UPDATE</th><th>Optimistic (version)</th><th>=
Redis lock</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=3D"hl"><td>Correct under races=
</td><td>=E2=9D=8C</td><td>=E2=9C=85</td><td>=E2=9C=85</td><td>=E2=9C=85</t=
d><td>=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F only with fencing</td></tr><tr><td>Round trips</td=
><td>2</td><td>2+</td><td>1</td><td>2 + retries</td><td>+2 to Redis</td></t=
r><tr><td>Behaviour under contention</td><td>wrong</td><td>queue</td><td>qu=
eue (short)</td><td>retry storms</td><td>queue</td></tr><tr><td>Extra depen=
dency</td><td>=E2=80=94</td><td>=E2=80=94</td><td>=E2=80=94</td><td>=E2=80=
=94</td><td>Redis</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class=3D"callout "><div class=3D"ct">=E2=9C=85 Our choice</div><p>Cond=
itional UPDATE for single-wallet debits; <code>SELECT =E2=80=A6 FOR UPDATE<=
/code> (in <code>wallet_id</code> order) when a transaction touches two wal=
lets on the same shard (Flow 1). Plus a <code>CHECK (balance_minor &gt;=3D =
held_minor)</code> constraint as a last line of defence. Isolation level st=
ays at InnoDB's default <code>REPEATABLE READ</code>: the safety comes from=
 locking reads, not from the isolation level.</p></div>
<div class=3D"callout tip"><div class=3D"ct">Follow-up: "Would SERIALIZABLE=
 fix the naive version?"</div><p>In InnoDB, <code>SERIALIZABLE</code> turns=
 plain <code>SELECT</code>s into shared-lock reads. Both requests take a sh=
ared lock, both try to upgrade to exclusive, and InnoDB detects a deadlock =
and kills one. Correct, but you pay with deadlock errors and retries. Takin=
g the exclusive lock directly is cleaner.</p></div>
