<ol class=3D"nl"><li><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><stro=
ng>The client creates the key</strong> once per user action (tap "Pay") and=
 sends the same key on every retry. A new tap =3D a new key.</p></div></li>=
<li><span class=3D"n">2</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>The key row is=
 part of the money transaction.</strong> Either both the movement and the k=
ey commit, or neither does. A separate "check Redis, then move money" step =
has a crash window between the two.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">3</=
span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Concurrent duplicates are handled by In=
noDB:</strong> the second <code>INSERT</code> of the same primary key block=
s on the first transaction's lock; if the first commits, the second gets <c=
ode>1062 Duplicate entry</code>; if the first rolls back, the second procee=
ds as if it were first.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">4</span><div cl=
ass=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Store the response</strong> and replay it, includin=
g failures that are final (<code>INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS</code>), so a retry get=
s the same answer instead of a second attempt that might now succeed.</p></=
div></li><li><span class=3D"n">5</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Same =
key, different body</strong> (compare <code>request_hash</code>) =E2=86=92 =
<code>409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED</code>. Protects against a client bug reus=
ing keys.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">6</span><div class=3D"li-b"><=
p><strong>Scope the key</strong> to the caller (<code>scope_id</code> =3D w=
allet or merchant), so two merchants can't collide. Purge after 7 days; the=
 transaction itself stays forever.</p></div></li></ol>
<h4>Idempotency all the way down</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table><thead><tr><th>Hop</th><th>Dedup key</th></tr></t=
head><tbody><tr><td>Client =E2=86=92 our API</td><td><code>Idempotency-Key<=
/code> header =E2=86=92 <code>idempotency_keys</code> row</td></tr><tr><td>=
Transfer saga T2 on the receiver's shard</td><td><code>applied_transfers.tx=
n_id</code> primary key</td></tr><tr><td>Us =E2=86=92 payment gateway</td><=
td>our <code>txn_id</code> as the order receipt; gateways dedup on it</td><=
/tr><tr><td>Gateway webhook =E2=86=92 us</td><td>conditional <code>status =
=3D 'PENDING' =E2=86=92 'COMPLETED'</code> transition</td></tr><tr><td>Us =
=E2=86=92 bank payout</td><td>our <code>txn_id</code> as the payout referen=
ce</td></tr><tr><td>Kafka =E2=86=92 consumers</td><td><code>event_id</code>=
; each consumer stores processed ids (or upserts)</td></tr></tbody></table>=
</div>
<div class=3D"callout interview"><div class=3D"ct">=F0=9F=92=AC Interview l=
ine</div><p>"Exactly-once is at-least-once delivery plus an idempotency key=
 stored in the same transaction as the money movement. Every hop after that=
 (saga steps, gateway, bank, Kafka consumers) has its own dedup key, so any=
 retry anywhere is harmless."</p></div>
