<h3 id=3D"deep-dive-8-a-big-merchant-receives-2000-payments-a-second-its-wa=
llet-row-is-the-bottleneck-what-do-you-do" class=3D"dd" data-toc=3D"Deep Di=
ve 8: Hot merchant wallets"><span class=3D"dd-n">Deep Dive 8</span><span cl=
ass=3D"dd-q">A big merchant receives 2,000 payments a second. Its wallet ro=
w is the bottleneck. What do you do?</span></h3>
<p>Every payment updates the merchant's <code>balance_minor</code>, so ever=
y payment waits for the same row lock. Each holder keeps the lock until its=
 commit is fsynced and (with semi-sync) acknowledged by the replica, roughl=
y 1=E2=80=933 ms, which caps one row at a few hundred to ~1,000 updates/s.<=
/p>
<h4 class=3D"approach"><span class=3D"ap-tag">Approach 1</span>Split the me=
rchant into N sub-wallets (bucketed balance)</h4>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- merchant 501 has 16 rows: (501, bucke=
t 0) =E2=80=A6 (501, bucket 15), all on the same shard</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> merchant_buckets <span class=3D"=
hljs-keyword">SET</span> balance_minor <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</s=
pan> balance_minor <span class=3D"hljs-operator">+</span> :amt
 <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> merchant_id <span class=3D"hljs-=
operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">501</span> <span class=3D"=
hljs-keyword">AND</span> bucket <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> :t=
xn_id <span class=3D"hljs-operator">%</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">16=
</span>;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- merchant balance =3D SUM over its 16 bucket=
s; payouts sweep buckets</span></code></pre></div>
<ol class=3D"nl"><li class=3D"pro"><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"=
li-b"><p><strong>Pros:</strong> 16=C3=97 the write throughput with no chang=
e to correctness; credits never need a balance check, so any bucket will do=
.</p></div></li><li class=3D"con"><span class=3D"n">2</span><div class=3D"l=
i-b"><p><strong>Cons:</strong> debits (refunds, payouts) must pick a bucket=
 with enough money or sweep first; balance reads sum 16 rows.</p></div></li=
></ol>
<h4 class=3D"approach"><span class=3D"ap-tag">Approach 2</span>Append now, =
apply in batches</h4>
<p>Insert the credit's ledger entry immediately (inserts don't contend on o=
ne row), and let a per-merchant worker fold pending entries into the balanc=
e every ~100 ms in one <code>UPDATE =E2=80=A6 + SUM(=E2=80=A6)</code>.</p>
<ol class=3D"nl"><li class=3D"pro"><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"=
li-b"><p><strong>Pros:</strong> one balance update per batch instead of per=
 payment.</p></div></li><li class=3D"con"><span class=3D"n">2</span><div cl=
ass=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Cons:</strong> merchant balance lags by the batch i=
nterval; refunds must count unapplied credits or wait.</p></div></li></ol>
<h4 class=3D"approach"><span class=3D"ap-tag">Approach 3</span>Credit async=
hronously through a queue</h4>
<ol class=3D"nl"><li class=3D"pro"><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"=
li-b"><p><strong>Pros:</strong> smooths spikes completely.</p></div></li><l=
i class=3D"con"><span class=3D"n">2</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Co=
ns:</strong> the payer is debited synchronously but the merchant credit is =
eventually consistent, and the clearing balance in between must be monitore=
d. Fine for merchants (they settle daily anyway), not for P2P.</p></div></l=
i></ol>
<div class=3D"callout "><div class=3D"ct">=E2=9C=85 Our choice</div><p>Buck=
eted balances for the few known hot merchants (configured per merchant, e.g=
. 16=E2=80=9364 buckets). Users never need it: a person can't make 1,000 pa=
yments a second. Only <strong>credits</strong> are spread; debits on a merc=
hant are rare and can take a short lock across buckets.</p></div>
<h3 id=3D"deep-dive-9-how-do-notifications-history-and-fraud-checks-learn-a=
bout-a-payment-without-ever-missing-or-inventing-one" class=3D"dd" data-toc=
=3D"Deep Dive 9: Reliable events: transactional outbox"><span class=3D"dd-n=
">Deep Dive 9</span><span class=3D"dd-q">How do notifications, history and =
fraud checks learn about a payment without ever missing or inventing one?</=
span></h3>
<p>The naive version, "commit to MySQL, then publish to Kafka", has a crash=
