<h3 id=3D"deep-dive-10-how-do-you-shard-the-wallets-and-how-do-you-add-shar=
ds-later" class=3D"dd" data-toc=3D"Deep Dive 10: Sharding &amp; resharding"=
><span class=3D"dd-n">Deep Dive 10</span><span class=3D"dd-q">How do you sh=
ard the wallets, and how do you add shards later?</span></h3>
<ol class=3D"nl"><li><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><stro=
ng>Shard key =3D <code>wallet_id</code>.</strong> Every single-wallet opera=
tion (debit, credit, history, idempotency) is then local. Sharding by user =
would work the same (one wallet per user), but merchants have several walle=
ts.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">2</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><str=
ong>Logical shards:</strong> <code>logical =3D hash(wallet_id) % 4096</code=
>, and a small directory maps the 4,096 logical shards onto 16 physical MyS=
QL clusters. Resharding moves whole logical shards (copy, catch up from bin=
log, brief write freeze, flip the directory), never re-hashes individual wa=
llets.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">3</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><=
strong>System accounts per shard:</strong> each physical shard has its own =
clearing accounts, so top-ups and withdrawals stay local and no system row =
is shared by all traffic.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">4</span><div =
class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Global ids:</strong> <code>txn_id</code> from a S=
nowflake-style generator (time + node + sequence), unique without coordinat=
ion.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">5</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><st=
rong>Cross-wallet queries</strong> (all transactions of a merchant group, f=
inance reports) run on the warehouse fed by Kafka, never by fanning out to =
every shard.</p></div></li></ol>
<h3 id=3D"deep-dive-11-a-shard-primary-dies-one-millisecond-after-confirmin=
g-a-payment-is-the-payment-lost" class=3D"dd" data-toc=3D"Deep Dive 11: Dur=
ability &amp; failover"><span class=3D"dd-n">Deep Dive 11</span><span class=
=3D"dd-q">A shard primary dies one millisecond after confirming a payment. =
Is the payment lost?</span></h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Value</th><th>Why<=
/th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>innodb_flush_log_at_trx_commit</code>=
</td><td><code>1</code></td><td>redo log fsynced at every commit; no commit=
ted transaction lost on a crash</td></tr><tr><td><code>sync_binlog</code></=
td><td><code>1</code></td><td>binlog fsynced at every commit, so replicas a=
nd CDC never miss a committed transaction</td></tr><tr><td>Semi-sync replic=
ation</td><td><code>AFTER_SYNC</code> (lossless)</td><td>the commit is ackn=
owledged only after at least one replica has the binlog event. Semi-sync si=
lently falls back to async if no replica answers within <code>rpl_semi_sync=
_source_timeout</code>: set it high and alert on fallback</td></tr><tr><td>=
Failover</td><td>Orchestrator / MySQL Group Replication</td><td>promote the=
 replica that has every acknowledged transaction; fence the old primary so =
it can't accept writes</td></tr><tr><td>Backups</td><td>daily physical back=
up + continuous binlog archive</td><td>point-in-time recovery (e.g. after a=
 bad deploy)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<ul class=3D"bl"><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>RPO =3D 0 within the re=
gion:</strong> anything we told the user "COMPLETED" is on at least two mac=
hines.</p></div></li><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>DR region:</strong>=
 asynchronous replication (a few seconds behind). After a regional failover=
, the last seconds may be missing; reconciliation against gateway / bank re=
cords and client-side receipts restores them. That's why the interviewer's =
RPO =3D 0 was scoped to one region.</p></div></li><li><div class=3D"li-b"><=
p><strong>No active-active writes</strong> for the same wallet in two regio=
ns: two regions could each approve the last =E2=82=B9500.</p></div></li></u=
l>
<h3 id=3D"deep-dive-12-how-do-you-prove-the-money-is-right-every-day" class=
=3D"dd" data-toc=3D"Deep Dive 12: Reconciliation &amp; audit"><span class=
=3D"dd-n">Deep Dive 12</span><span class=3D"dd-q">How do you prove the mone=
y is right, every day?</span></h3>
<h4>Internal checks (our books agree with themselves)</h4>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- 1. every transaction balances</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> txn_id <span class=3D"hljs-keywo=
rd">FROM</span> ledger_entries
 <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">GROUP</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">BY<=
/span> txn_id
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">HAVING</span> <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">SU=
M</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CASE</span> direction <span class=3D"=
hljs-keyword">WHEN</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;DEBIT&#x27;</sp=
an> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">THEN</span> amount_minor <span class=3D"hl=
js-keyword">ELSE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">-</span>amount_minor =
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">END</span>) <span class=3D"hljs-operator">&lt;=
&gt;</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">0</span>;

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- 2. cached balance =3D sum of entries (run i=
ncrementally from the last checked entry_id)</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> w.wallet_id <span class=3D"hljs-=
keyword">FROM</span> wallets w
  <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">JOIN</span> (<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SE=
LECT</span> wallet_id, <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">SUM</span>(<span class=
=3D"hljs-keyword">CASE</span> direction <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHEN</=
span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;CREDIT&#x27;</span> <span class=3D"=
hljs-keyword">THEN</span> amount_minor <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ELSE</s=
pan> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">-</span>amount_minor <span class=3D"hljs=
-keyword">END</span>) s
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</span> ledger_entries <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-keyword">GROUP</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">BY</span> wal=
let_id) l <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">USING</span> (wallet_id)
 <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> w.type <span class=3D"hljs-opera=
tor">&lt;&gt;</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;SYSTEM&#x27;</span> =
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">AND</span> w.balance_minor <span class=3D"hljs=
-operator">&lt;&gt;</span> l.s;

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- 3. money in flight: transfer_clearing summe=
d over all shards =3D open transfers&#x27; amounts</span></code></pre></div=
>
<h4>External checks (our books agree with the outside world)</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table><thead><tr><th>Compare</th><th>With</th><th>Typic=
al break</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Completed top-ups per day</td><td>=
gateway settlement file</td><td>payment captured but never credited (webhoo=
k + poller both missed it)</td></tr><tr><td>Completed withdrawals</td><td>b=
ank statement / payout report (UTRs)</td><td>payout we think failed actuall=
y succeeded, or a late return</td></tr><tr><td><code>gateway_clearing</code=
> balance</td><td>money the gateway actually transferred to our bank (T+1)<=
/td><td>fees, chargebacks</td></tr><tr><td>Total user balances</td><td>mone=
y held in our escrow / nodal bank account</td><td>any of the above</td></tr=
></tbody></table></div>
<ul class=3D"bl"><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p>Every mismatch becomes a "break=
" in an ops queue; fixes are new, approved transactions (<strong>maker=E2=
=80=93checker</strong>: one person proposes, another approves), never edits=
.</p></div></li><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p>Stuck states are alerts too: tra=
nsfers in <code>DEBITED</code> &gt; 5 min, withdrawals <code>PROCESSING</co=
de> &gt; 24 h, top-ups <code>PENDING</code> with a captured payment.</p></d=
iv></li><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p>Ledger immutability: the app's DB user h=
as only <code>INSERT</code> / <code>SELECT</code> on <code>ledger_entries</=
code>; monthly partitions are archived to write-once object storage.</p></d=
iv></li></ul>
<h3 id=3D"deep-dive-13-how-do-you-enforce-limits-stop-fraud-and-secure-the-=
wallet" class=3D"dd" data-toc=3D"Deep Dive 13: Limits, fraud &amp; security=
"><span class=3D"dd-n">Deep Dive 13</span><span class=3D"dd-q">How do you e=
nforce limits, stop fraud and secure the wallet?</span></h3>
<h4>Limits checked inside the money transaction</h4>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- daily outflow: one counter row per wa=
llet per day, on the wallet&#x27;s shard, same transaction as the debit</sp=
an>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> IGNORE <span class=3D"hljs-keywo=
rd">INTO</span> daily_usage (wallet_id, <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">day</s=
pan>, out_minor) <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> (:w, <span clas=
s=3D"hljs-built_in">CURRENT_DATE</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">0</spa=
n>);
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> daily_usage <span class=3D"hljs-=
keyword">SET</span> out_minor <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> out_=
minor <span class=3D"hljs-operator">+</span> :amt
 <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> wallet_id <span class=3D"hljs-op=
erator">=3D</span> :w <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">AND</span> <span class=
=3D"hljs-keyword">day</span> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span=
 class=3D"hljs-built_in">CURRENT_DATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">A=
ND</span> out_minor <span class=3D"hljs-operator">+</span> :amt <span class=
=3D"hljs-operator">&lt;=3D</span> :daily_cap;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- 0 rows =E2=86=92 LIMIT_EXCEEDED =E2=86=92 R=
OLLBACK (the row lock also serializes two concurrent debits)</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- balance cap on credit: the receiver&#x27;s =
UPDATE has &quot;balance_minor + :amt &lt;=3D :kyc_cap&quot; (Flow 1)</span=
></code></pre></div>
<p>Limits checked outside the transaction (a Redis counter, say) have the s=
ame race as the naive balance check: two requests both read "=E2=82=B99,000=
 of =E2=82=B910,000 used" and both pass.</p>
<h4>Fraud</h4>
<ul class=3D"bl"><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Synchronous risk check<=
/strong> before high-risk debits (new device, new payee, large amount, unus=
ual hour): a fast rules + model score; high score =E2=86=92 step-up (MPIN /=
 OTP) or block.</p></div></li><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Asynchrono=
us scoring</strong> on the Kafka stream: velocity (10 payees in 5 minutes),=
 mule patterns (money in, immediately out to a bank) =E2=86=92 freeze the w=
allet (<code>status =3D 'FROZEN'</code>; the debit <code>UPDATE</code> alre=
ady requires <code>ACTIVE</code>).</p></div></li><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p=
><strong>New-device cooling period</strong>: lower limits for the first 24 =
h after a device or SIM change.</p></div></li></ul>
<h4>Security</h4>
<ul class=3D"bl"><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p>OAuth access tokens bound to a =
registered device; MPIN or biometric for debits above a threshold.</p></div=
></li><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p>Bank account numbers and KYC documents enc=
rypted at rest (envelope encryption, KMS); masked in logs and APIs.</p></di=
v></li><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p>Card data never touches us: the gateway t=
okenizes it (keeps us out of most PCI scope).</p></div></li><li><div class=
=3D"li-b"><p>Webhooks: HMAC signature + timestamp (reject replays) + status=
 re-fetch; bank APIs over mTLS.</p></div></li><li><div class=3D"li-b"><p>Ad=
min tools: every manual adjustment is a ledger transaction with maker=E2=80=
=93checker approval and an audit trail.</p></div></li></ul>
</section>

<section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"failure-scenarios-cheat-sheet" data-toc=3D=
"9. Failure Cheat Sheet"><span class=3D"sec-n">9.</span> Failure Scenarios =
Cheat Sheet</h2>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table><thead><tr><th>What fails</th><th>What the system=
 does</th><th>Money safe because</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Client ret=
ries / double tap</td><td>second request hits the same idempotency key =E2=
=86=92 stored response</td><td>key row is in the money transaction</td></tr=
><tr><td>Two debits race on one wallet</td><td>second waits on the row lock=
, then fails the balance condition</td><td>conditional UPDATE + CHECK const=
raint</td></tr><tr><td>Deadlock between two transfers</td><td>InnoDB rolls =
one back; we retry</td><td>id-ordered locking; idempotent retry</td></tr><t=
r><td>Crash between saga T1 and T2</td><td>recovery worker retries T2 (dedu=
p by <code>applied_transfers</code>)</td><td>money sits in <code>transfer_c=
learing</code>, visible to reconciliation</td></tr><tr><td>Receiver wallet =
frozen mid-saga</td><td>compensate: credit sender back</td><td>T2 fails per=
manently, never on a timeout</td></tr><tr><td>2PC coordinator crash (if XA =
used)</td><td>recovery reads its log: COMMIT =E2=86=92 re-send, none =E2=86=
=92 rollback</td><td>decision is durable before phase 2</td></tr><tr><td>Sh=
ard primary dies</td><td>semi-sync replica promoted, old primary fenced</td=
><td>commit acknowledged only after the replica has it</td></tr><tr><td>Gat=
eway webhook lost / duplicated</td><td>poller + conditional PENDING =E2=86=
=92 COMPLETED</td><td>state transition happens once</td></tr><tr><td>Bank p=
ayout timeout</td><td>stay PROCESSING, poll status by reference</td><td>nev=
er refund or re-send on a timeout</td></tr><tr><td>Kafka down</td><td>outbo=
x rows accumulate; relay catches up</td><td>events come from committed rows=
 only</td></tr><tr><td>Hot merchant spike</td><td>credits spread over bucke=
ts</td><td>no single row takes all the locks</td></tr></tbody></table></div=
>
</section>

<section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"quick-revision" data-toc=3D"10. Quick Revi=
sion"><span class=3D"sec-n">10.</span> Quick Revision</h2>
<ol class=3D"nl"><li><span class=3D"n">1</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><stro=
ng>Store money as integers (paise)</strong> in a <strong>double-entry, appe=
nd-only ledger</strong>; the wallet balance is a cached sum updated in the =
same transaction.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">2</span><div class=3D=
"li-b"><p><strong>No double spend:</strong> <code>UPDATE =E2=80=A6 SET bala=
nce =3D balance =E2=88=92 x WHERE balance =E2=88=92 held =E2=89=A5 x</code>=
 (atomic check-and-debit under a row lock) + <code>CHECK</code> constraint.=
</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">3</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong=
>Two wallets, one shard:</strong> lock both in <code>wallet_id</code> order=
 (no deadlocks), one local transaction, retry on 1213 / 1205.</p></div></li=
><li><span class=3D"n">4</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Exactly-once:=
</strong> <code>Idempotency-Key</code> row inside the money transaction; de=
dup keys on every hop (saga step, gateway, bank, Kafka).</p></div></li><li>=
<span class=3D"n">5</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Cross-shard:</stro=
ng> saga =E2=80=94 debit into a per-shard clearing account, idempotent cred=
it on the other shard, durable state machine, retry forward, compensate onl=
y on permanent failure. <strong>2PC (XA)</strong> gives isolation but holds=
 locks between prepare and commit and blocks if the coordinator dies.</p></=
div></li><li><span class=3D"n">6</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Exter=
nal money:</strong> pending row first; credit only after the gateway confir=
ms; withdrawals reserve first and treat timeouts as unknown, never as failu=
re.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">7</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><str=
ong>Events:</strong> transactional outbox =E2=86=92 CDC =E2=86=92 Kafka key=
ed by wallet; consumers dedup by event id.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D=
"n">8</span><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Scale:</strong> shard by <code>w=
allet_id</code> (logical shards =E2=86=92 physical), bucket hot merchant ba=
lances, history from a read model.</p></div></li><li><span class=3D"n">9</s=
pan><div class=3D"li-b"><p><strong>Prove it daily:</strong> every transacti=
on sums to zero, balances equal their entries, clearing accounts match in-f=
light work, and our totals match gateway and bank files.</p></div></li></ol=
>
</section>
